  <section class="faith-intro">
    <div class="container container-narrow">
      <details class="faith-intro-disclosure" data-faith-intro>
        <summary class="faith-intro-summary">
          <span class="faith-intro-summary-label" data-faith-intro-label>Read introduction</span>
          <span class="faith-intro-summary-chev" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </summary>
        <div class="faith-intro-body">
          <p class="faith-intro-prose hero-excerpt-dropcap">On the Sole Government of God is a treatise attributed to Justin Martyr that marshals the testimony of Greek poets and philosophers to argue for monotheism. The author shows that Homer, Sophocles, Pythagoras, Plato, and others all acknowledged, however dimly, a single supreme deity. The argument is simple: the best minds of Greece confirm what the Christians openly confess.</p>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>
    
